{"term":"elder","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:78a5407646621dfc5f","definition":"comparative degree of old: older, greater than another in age or seniority.","example":"It's typical for elder married couples to live in retirement homes.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["geriatric","long in the tooth","on in years"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"comparative, form-of","register":"comparative, form-of","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:014b0d7026edbb8ae5","definition":"Closer to the dealer, i.e. receiving cards earlier than others.","example":"The deal fell to Copling and the automaton therefore had the first \"elder hand,\" with the advantage of a discard of five cards against its opponent's three.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["senior"],"antonyms":["junior","younger"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7c55f8c63a00862d5c","definition":"A leader or senior member of a tribe or community, often of considerable age, respected as an authority figure, especially in a counselling, consultative, or ceremonial role.","example":"We were presented to the village elder.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["mzee","senior","forerunner"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fa14215f1676cedbe0","definition":"An old person.","example":"Treating illness among society’s elders is challenging since board-certified geriatricians (physicians trained, knowledgeable and certified in treating older patients) are in short supply, here in El Paso and throughout the country.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["eld"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US","register":"US","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0be6df125aeaa52b9f","definition":"One who is older than another.","example":"Respect your elders.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["mzee","senior","forerunner"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"in-plural, relational","register":"in-plural, relational","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6721b9cb67339362b5","definition":"One who lived at an earlier period; a predecessor.","example":"Carry your Head[…] as your Elders have done.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["antecessor"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4636d199d4709dcff8","definition":"An officer of a church, sometimes having teaching responsibilities.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["mzee","senior","forerunner"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c20b2942a2b5d50564","definition":"A clergyman authorized to administer all the sacraments.","example":"a travelling elder","pos":"noun","synonyms":["mzee","senior","forerunner"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via 